.IX Title "Structs 3pm"
.TH Structs 3pm "2026-03-26" "perl v5.36.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
POSIX::Structs \- FFI::C definitions of common POSIX/Linux structs
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&  use POSIX::Structs qw( POSIX::Structs::Stat POSIX::Structs::Timespec );
\&
\&  my $st = POSIX::Structs::Stat\->new;
\&  fstatat($dirfd, "file", $st, 0);
\&  printf "mode=0%o  size=%d\en", $st\->st_mode & 07777, $st\->st_size;
\&
\&  my $ts = POSIX::Structs::Timespec\->new;
\&  $ts\->tv_sec(1_000_000_000);
\&  $ts\->tv_nsec(0);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
POSIX::Structs provides \s-1FFI::C\s0 struct definitions for the common C
structs used by \s-1POSIX\s0 and Linux syscalls.  All layouts are for
x86_64 Linux; other architectures are not currently supported.
.PP
The following packages are defined and may be imported by name:
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Stat""      — ""struct stat""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Stat\fR      — \f(CWstruct stat\fR" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Stat — struct stat"
.PD 0
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Timespec""  — ""struct timespec""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Timespec\fR  — \f(CWstruct timespec\fR" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Timespec — struct timespec"
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Timeval""   — ""struct timeval""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Timeval\fR   — \f(CWstruct timeval\fR" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Timeval — struct timeval"
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Dirent""    — ""struct dirent"" (d_name fixed at 256 bytes)" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Dirent\fR    — \f(CWstruct dirent\fR (d_name fixed at 256 bytes)" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Dirent — struct dirent (d_name fixed at 256 bytes)"
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Iovec""     — ""struct iovec""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Iovec\fR     — \f(CWstruct iovec\fR" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Iovec — struct iovec"
.ie n .IP """POSIX::Structs::Flock""     — ""struct flock""" 4
.el .IP "\f(CWPOSIX::Structs::Flock\fR     — \f(CWstruct flock\fR" 4
.IX Item "POSIX::Structs::Flock — struct flock"
.PD
.PP
The shared FFI::Platypus instance used to define these types is
accessible via \f(CW\*(C`POSIX::Structs::ffi()\*(C'\fR.  Modules that need to attach
additional functions should use this instance so that the struct types
are visible to their \f(CW\*(C`attach()\*(C'\fR calls.
.SH "PORTABILITY"
.IX Header "PORTABILITY"
The struct layouts are hard-coded for x86_64 Linux.  Contributions
for other architectures are welcome.
